{
	"name": "Slumber Potion",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/magic/control/sleep-bubble-purple.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Anyone using one of your potions can apply it to a weapon or food as a bonus action. Applying a potion to an unwilling target requires you to grapple with, or successfully grab on, your target, but allows you to use an action to force-feed the target on a failed Constitution save.</p><p>A creature who drinks this potion falls into a torporous slumber for at least one hour and up to 20 years if they choose when they drink the potion. A creature in such a magical slumber cannot be awakened by traditional means, though @UUID[Compendium.a5e.a5e-spells.Item.l16wg9h1z9s16exb]{Remove Curse} and more powerful magics can awaken them, as can true love’s kiss. They do not hunger, thirst, or require air while in this state, but still cannot go into a bag of holding.</p>",
